id: pm-gh1072
title: "GH-1072: pm install leaks user allow-scripts config into isolated package installs"
description: GitHub issue #1072 reports that a non-empty user-level npm allow-scripts setting leaks into pm-owned isolated installs and makes npm reject an otherwise valid package despite --ignore-scripts.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:packages",configuration-isolation,github,security
created_at: "2026-08-21T05:41:50.945Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:48.474Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:47.951Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T17:49:47.951Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Sanitize inherited npm configuration for pm-owned installs without weakening --ignore-scripts; cover npm and packed npx/bunx installs with an ambient allow-scripts negative control; return an actionable structured error for truly invalid package policy; preserve project/global package isolation.
parent: pm-tnud
severity: high
repro_steps: Configure user npm allow-scripts; initialize a fresh tracker; install a valid packed extension through npx with --project; observe npm EALLOWSCRIPTS.
resolution: "Resolved: pm-owned npm installs isolate ambient allow-scripts while preserving ignore-scripts and required environment configuration."
expected_result: Package installation runs inside a sanitized npm configuration boundary while pm remains authoritative for lifecycle-script policy.
actual_result: Ambient user allow-scripts reaches the subprocess and aborts the install before activation.
affected_version: 2026.8.20
component: package installer
